{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"6d00000000000001","type":"text","x":0,"y":-380,"width":3130,"height":250,"text":"<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## Bipartite matching and Hall’s theorem\nFor finite simple graphs, first distinguish allowed pairs, selected pairs and required coverage. Read the first two rows for existence and improvement; the third connects search certificates with modelling choices. The lower rows introduce flow capacities and preference stability. Click a title for its full explanation.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n二分图匹配与 Hall 定理：先区分允许配对、选中配对与覆盖要求。前两行读存在性与增广机制；第三行读搜索证书与建模选择；下方两行分别补网络流容量与偏好稳定性的定义。普通匹配以有限简单图为范围；流模型与稳定模型的附加条件见各卡。点击标题阅读完整讲解。"},
		{"id":"6d00000000000002","type":"text","x":0,"y":0,"width":520,"height":270,"text":"<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[二分图配对关系|Allowed pairings]]\nGive the two sides of a [[二分图|bipartite graph]] their roles. An edge records eligibility, before any assignment is chosen.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n为[[二分图]]两侧指定角色。边先记录资格，尚未决定最终分配。","color":"5"},
		{"id":"6d00000000000003","type":"text","x":870,"y":0,"width":520,"height":270,"text":"<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[匹配定义|Matching]]\nSelect a set of allowed edges with no shared endpoint. Each object is used at most once.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n从允许边中选择端点互不重复的边集；每个对象至多用一次。","color":"5"},
		{"id":"6d00000000000004","type":"text","x":1740,"y":0,"width":520,"height":270,"text":"<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[左侧覆盖与完美匹配|Coverage and perfectness]]\nLeft coverage includes every left vertex. A perfect matching covers both sides; equal finite side sizes make left coverage perfect.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n左侧覆盖包含全部左点；完美匹配覆盖两侧。有限等大两侧中，左覆盖即完美。","color":"3"},
		{"id":"6d00000000000005","type":"text","x":2610,"y":0,"width":520,"height":270,"text":"<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[Hall 定理|Hall’s theorem]]\nLeft coverage exists exactly when every left subset has at least as many distinct neighbors as members. Neighbors form a union of options.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n覆盖左侧当且仅当每个左侧子集的不同邻居数不少于自身人数；邻居集是选项的并集。","color":"4"},
		{"id":"6d00000000000006","type":"text","x":0,"y":460,"width":520,"height":270,"text":"<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[极大与最大匹配|Maximal and maximum]]\nMaximal: no single edge can be added. Maximum: no matching has more edges. A maximal matching may still improve by replacing edges.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n极大：不能直接加边。最大：不存在边数更多的匹配。极大匹配仍可能通过换边改进。","color":"3"},
		{"id":"6d00000000000007","type":"text","x":870,"y":460,"width":520,"height":270,"text":"<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[增广路定义|Augmenting paths]]\nFor a fixed matching, take a simple path between two distinct unmatched vertices, alternating unselected and selected edges.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n相对固定匹配，简单路径两端为不同的未匹配点，沿路未选边与已选边交替。","color":"5"},
		{"id":"6d00000000000008","type":"text","x":1740,"y":460,"width":520,"height":270,"text":"<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[增广路对称差|Flipping an augmenting path]]\nRemove the path’s selected edges and add its unselected edges. Edges outside the path stay. The result is a matching larger by one.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n撤去路上已选边、加入未选边，路外保持不变；结果仍是匹配，边数恰增一。","color":"4"},
		{"id":"6d00000000000009","type":"text","x":2610,"y":460,"width":520,"height":270,"text":"<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[Berge最大匹配定理|Berge’s theorem]]\nA matching in a finite graph is maximum exactly when no augmenting path exists. The criterion also applies beyond bipartite graphs.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n有限图的匹配最大，当且仅当不存在增广路。判据也适用于非二分图。","color":"4"},
		{"id":"6d0000000000000a","type":"text","x":870,"y":920,"width":520,"height":270,"text":"<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[交替搜索的增广与缺额证书|Alternating search]]\nFix the matching and start at all unmatched left vertices. Find an augmenting path, or exhaust the search to obtain a deficient set. No roots means left coverage.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n固定匹配，从全部未匹配左点出发。找到增广路，或穷尽搜索后得到缺额集合；没有起点表示已覆盖左侧。","color":"6"},
		{"id":"6d0000000000000b","type":"text","x":0,"y":920,"width":520,"height":270,"text":"<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[Hall 缺额证书|Hall deficiency certificates]]\nA left set with fewer neighbors than members proves that full left coverage is impossible. Count its entire neighbor union.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n找到邻居数少于自身人数的左侧集合，即证明无法覆盖左侧；必须数完整邻居并集。","color":"1"},
		{"id":"6d0000000000000c","type":"text","x":2610,"y":920,"width":520,"height":270,"text":"<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[匹配建模要素|Modelling an assignment]]\nState both roles, allowed pairs, required coverage, capacities and the objective. One student–project example connects all five choices.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n写清双方角色、允许配对、覆盖对象、容量和目标；用同一学生—项目例贯穿五项选择。","color":"6"},
		{"id":"6d0000000000000d","type":"text","x":1740,"y":1380,"width":520,"height":270,"text":"<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[整数容量的槽化与网络流|Capacity: slots and flow]]\nWith unit demand and interchangeable integer places, cloning slots or using integral flow preserves valid assignments and their sizes.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n单位需求、可互换整数名额下，拆槽或整数流保留合法分配及已分配人数。","color":"4"},
		{"id":"6d0000000000000e","type":"text","x":1740,"y":920,"width":520,"height":270,"text":"<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[Hall 条件与带权最优|Feasibility and weighted cost]]\nHall tests whether left coverage exists. To compare costs, specify an objective over those feasible assignments. Changing costs can change the best choice.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\nHall 判断覆盖是否存在；比较成本须在可行分配上另定目标。改成本可能改变最优选择。","color":"3"},
		{"id":"6d0000000000000f","type":"text","x":1740,"y":1840,"width":520,"height":270,"text":"<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[稳定匹配与普通匹配|Feasibility and stability]]\nAllowed edges determine feasibility; two-sided rankings determine blocking pairs. A perfect minimum-cost matching may still be unstable.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n允许边决定可行性；双边排序决定阻挡对。最低成本完美匹配仍可能不稳定。","color":"3"},
		{"id":"matching-network-flow","type":"text","x":0,"y":1380,"width":520,"height":270,"text":"<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[网络流|Network flow]]\nNonnegative arc amounts obey capacities and conservation at intermediate vertices. Flow value is net transfer from source to sink.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n弧上非负数量遵守容量与中间点守恒；流值计算从源点到汇点的净运输量。","color":"5"},
		{"id":"matching-flow-integrality","type":"text","x":870,"y":1380,"width":520,"height":270,"text":"<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[最大流整数性|Maximum-flow integrality]]\nFinite networks with nonnegative integer capacities have an integral maximum flow. Some other optimal flows can still be fractional.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n有限网络若容量为非负整数，就存在整数最大流；其他最优流仍可能含分数。","color":"4"},
		{"id":"matching-blocking-pair","type":"text","x":0,"y":1840,"width":520,"height":270,"text":"<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[阻挡对|Blocking pairs]]\nIn the complete strict one-to-one model, an unselected pair blocks when both prefer each other to their current partners.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n完整严格一对一模型中，未彼此配对的两人都更喜欢对方而非现任伙伴，就形成阻挡对。","color":"5"},
		{"id":"matching-stable-definition","type":"text","x":870,"y":1840,"width":520,"height":270,"text":"<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[稳定匹配|Stable matching]]\nIn this finite equal-size complete strict model, a stable outcome is a perfect matching with no blocking pair.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n在有限等大、完整严格偏好模型中，稳定结果是没有阻挡对的完美匹配。","color":"5"}
	],
